#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some Fundamentals"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwrite; is very simple to use. Anyone that has used a text editor should "
"have no problems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:10
#, no-c-format
msgid "Drag and Drop"
msgstr "\"Dregen un droppen\""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwrite; uses the &kde; Drag and Drop protocol. Files may be dragged and "
"dropped onto &kwrite; from the Desktop, the filemanager &dolphin;, or some "
"remote &FTP; site opened in one of &dolphin;'s windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Line Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Though &kwrite; may most often be started from the &kde; program menu, or a "
"desktop icon, it can also be opened at the command line prompt of a terminal "
"window. There are a few useful options that are available when doing this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specify a File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By specifying the path and name of a particular file the user can have "
"&kwrite; open (or create) that file immediately upon startup. This option "
"might look something like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: fundamentals.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kwrite</command>\n"
"<option><replaceable>/home/myhome/docs/myfile.txt</replaceable></option>\n"
"</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specify a file on the Internet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The above-mentioned method could even be used to open files on the Internet "
"(if the user has an active connection at the time.) An example of this might "
"look like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: fundamentals.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kwrite</command>\n"
"<option><replaceable>ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/README</replaceable>\n"
"</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other Command Line Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following command line help options are available"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "This lists the most basic options available at the command line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help-qt</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This lists the options available for changing the way &kwrite; interacts "
"with &Qt;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help-kde</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This lists the options available for changing the way &kwrite; interacts "
"with &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help-all</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "This lists all of the command line options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--author</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lists &kwrite;'s authors in the terminal window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>-v, --version</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Lists version information for &Qt;, &kde;, and &kwrite;. Also available "
"through <userinput><command>kwrite</command> <option>-v</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>&kwrite;</command> <option>--license</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows license information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--stdin</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Causes &kwrite; to read the document content from STDIN. This is similar to "
"the common option <option>-</option> used in many command line programs, and "
"allows you to pipe command output into &kwrite;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kwrite</command> <option>--encoding</option> <parameter>encoding</"
"parameter> <parameter>&URL;</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Causes &kwrite; to use the specified encoding for the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kwrite</command> <option>--line</option> <parameter>line</"
"parameter> <parameter>&URL;</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigate to the specified line after opening the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: fundamentals.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kwrite</command> <option>--column</option> <parameter>column</"
"parameter> <parameter>&URL;</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigate to the specified column after opening the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: fundamentals.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Many of the shortcuts are configurable by way of the <link linkend=\"settings"
"\">Settings</link> menu. By default &kwrite; honors the following shortcuts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keycap
#: fundamentals.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keycap>Ins</keycap>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: fundamentals.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggle between Insert and Overwrite mode. When in insert mode the editor "
"will add any typed characters to the text while pushing along any data to "
"the right of the text cursor. Overwrite mode causes the entry of each "
"character to eliminate the character immediately to the right of the text "
"cursor."
msgstr ""

